From 4a57181dc2e0778996a9c9869dca9d2c43ecfe1c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 14:47:41 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] aimesh: the firmware-upgrade contract, the node version
 string, the setup notice

Reaper's firmware scripts now follow the stock ones in the GPL tree.
reaper_webs_upgrade.sh reads $1 like stock ssl_webs_upgrade.sh: with 1
(a mesh-wide upgrade, run on every unit) it downloads and verifies only,
sets cfg_fwstatus=6, fwpath=2, upgrade=1 and leaves the flash to AiMesh;
it used to flash and reboot the main router mid mesh upgrade.
reaper_webs_update.sh writes webs_state_info as 3006_102_8_Reaper_v<ver>,
the stock firmbase_firmver_buildno_extendno layout the watchdog notice and
the stock pages read (nodes showed "3.0.0.6.Reaper_v..."); a mesh-started
check is logged. The firmware page takes the mesh path whenever nodes are
registered (it was forced off). AiMesh.asp says AiMesh starts once setup
is done (rc starts the controller only with x_Setting or cfg_master) and
links the setup box (RAMS_10, in the packs commit). httpd: the aimesh:
onboarding lines are throttled to one per node and kind every 10 min, and
the "partial" line says it is normal. Lean: test_aimesh_interop.py.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
